{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race data, so this is a conservative baseline built from the contract, not a tuned design. Geometry: five line sensors spaced 2 cm apart across the front (x = -0.04 to +0.04, y = 0.05 m ahead of the axle), so the line stays in view through the bends and the sensors do not all lose it at once. Sensor size is 12 mm, which is smaller than the 25 mm tape, so readings change sharply with lateral offset. Wheel track 0.12 m and radius 0.03 m give a moderate turn authority. Mass 0.8 kg and body length 0.16 m keep the yaw inertia modest. Body width 0.12 m leaves the off-track limit at 0.06 m. Controller: sensor weights are proportional to sensor x (-1, -0.5, 0, 0.5, 1), so signal is about the line offset in units of the sensor spacing and stays within ±1. kp = 4 gives roughly 1400 PWM of differential per unit of signal, which should correct a 3 cm offset quickly without saturating. kd = 0.3 damps the oscillation expected from a high kp. ki = 0.05 is small because the integral term is mainly a risk on a curve. base_speed = 1.6 (about 80 percent of full PWM) aims to cover roughly 4.5 m in under 3 s. line_loss = last_direction, so a robot that drifts off the tape turns back toward the side it last saw the line. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with rms_error around 0.02 m. The slalom may show the most oscillation. Next measurements needed: completion time (to test whether base_speed can rise), steering_oscillation (to tune kd), and line_loss_events (to check whether line_loss handling is needed on tight bends).",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.6,
    "kp": 4.0,
    "ki": 0.05,
    "kd": 0.3,
    "sensor_weights": [-1.0, -0.5, 0.0, 0.5, 1.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor line PD",
      "notes": "Conservative first candidate: five 12 mm sensors spaced 2 cm across the front, proportional weights, kp 4, kd 0.3, base speed 1.6, last-direction line recovery. No race data yet, so values come from the contract's scales and are expected to be refined after the first race."
    }
  }
}
